Chapter: DhcpRenew
  cites Net chapter DhcpIO
  cites Net chapter NetDriver
  cites Net chapter NetworkConfig
  cites Kernel chapter Hpet

 A lease is a loan, and this is the test that it is asked for again. The
 acquisition test proves an address arrives; nothing in it would notice a
 client that took one and held it forever, which is what this tree did
 until 2026-07-30.

 IT NEEDS A SHORT LEASE TO BE A TEST AT ALL. Renewal happens at half the
 lease, so against the default hour nothing observable happens inside a
 run: the sidecar asks codex-vm for a four-second lease, T1 is two
 seconds, and the spin below covers it several times over.

 THE ROWS ARE CHOSEN SO A CLIENT THAT DOES NOTHING FAILS THEM. `due
 before` must be no, because a lease taken a moment ago is not due, and a
 test whose first row was already yes would pass on a broken clock. `due
 after wait` must be yes, or the spin did not outlast T1 and the renewal
 that follows proves nothing. `renewed` compares lease-start, which only
 an accepted ACK moves.

Section: Waiting

 The wait is a spin on the clock rather than a count of turns, because
 what has to elapse is SECONDS and the turns-per-second of this loop is
 whatever the machine happens to give. Each turn reads the HPET, which
 is a VM exit, so the host advances its models and can answer.

  spin-until : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  spin-until (deadline) (fuel) =
    if fuel <= 0 then hpet-seconds
    else if hpet-seconds >= deadline then hpet-seconds
    else spin-until deadline (fuel - 1)

Section: Entry

  yn : Boolean -> Text
  yn (b) = if b then "yes" else "no"

  opening : [Console, Network.Read, Network.Write] Nothing = act
    let card = net-driver-bring-up
    in let mac = net-driver-mac
    in act
      cfg <- dhcp-io-configure mac "codex" 305419896 200000 hpet-seconds
      print-line-uni ("leased      : " & yn (net-is-configured cfg))
      print-line-uni ("lease time  : " & show (cfg.lease-time))
      print-line-uni ("due before  : " & yn (net-lease-due cfg hpet-seconds))
      let waited = spin-until (cfg.lease-start + cfg.lease-time / 2 + 1) 20000000
      in act
        print-line-uni ("due after   : " & yn (net-lease-due cfg waited))
        cfg2 <- dhcp-io-maybe-renew cfg 305419897 200000 waited
        print-line-uni ("renewed     : " & yn (cfg2.lease-start /= cfg.lease-start))
        print-line-uni ("address held: " & yn (net-is-configured cfg2))
      end
    end
  end

